# two-plane-allow — control-plane code that holds planning data today, or calls a lifecycle
# record a bead. One `<path>:<what> <removed-by>` per line; blank lines and `#` comments are
# ignored. `<what>` is the finding's name: `table`, `table.column`, `Type.field`, `Type`, a
# key prefix such as `"bead/"`, or the planning word a SQL literal carries.
#
# SHRINK-ONLY. `<removed-by>` is the work item whose landing deletes the code, and the line
# leaves this list in that change. A line that no longer matches a finding is itself a
# finding, so the list stays exact. `kept <why>` marks a name that only collides with a
# planning word.
#
# Seeded at authorship (sp-k2cghb) from the tree. spira-lc's dolt reads and the copied columns
# go with spira-lc on the state-store contract (sp-s6o3wx).
lifecycle/src/batch.rs:BatchRow.parent kept a round's parent round, not a bead's parent edge
spira-lc/src/control/bridge/topics.rs:"bead/" kept the broker topic families bead/<id>/state and bead/<id>/sessions: published names, not record keys
